{%- comment -%}
  Resolve an image value that came out of a section setting.

  Sections in this theme take image URLs as plain text so the same field can hold
  either a remote CDN URL or a file that ships with the theme. This snippet
  decides which: anything containing "://" or starting with "//" is passed
  through untouched; anything else is treated as a theme asset filename and run
  through asset_url. That keeps every Pinemoor photograph inside the theme zip —
  no dependency on a CDN that might be cleaned out later — while still allowing
  a Shopify Files URL to be pasted into the theme editor.

  Usage: {%- render 'pm-img-src', src: section.settings.image_1 -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign v = src | strip
  if v == blank
    echo ''
  elsif v contains '://'
    echo v
  elsif v contains '//'
    echo v
  else
    echo v | asset_url
  endif
-%}
